=== parameters ===
alpha=0.05 VaR; lookback L=252 for hist/param; MC paths=5000; Kupiec LR on exceptions
all risk estimates use only past returns (shift so day-t VaR uses data through t-1)
cite: Kupiec 1995 J. Derivatives — Techniques for verifying the accuracy of risk measurement models
cite: Artzner et al. 1999 Math. Finance — Coherent measures of risk (CVaR/ES motivation)
cite: lag all estimates — no look-ahead into same-day PnL

=== VaR backtest (Kupiec) ===
n=1247 hist_exceptions=73 rate=0.0585 (target 0.05) LR=1.820 p=0.177
n=1247 para_exceptions=67 rate=0.0537 (target 0.05) LR=0.357 p=0.550
mean_hist_VaR=0.0270 mean_CVaR=0.0337 CVaR>=VaR check=1.00 (finite days only; expect 1.00)
MC_t5 VaR=0.0298 CVaR=0.0423

=== stress tests (scenario PnL) ===
stress equity_-10pct: book_pnl=-0.0525
stress rates_+100bp_proxy: book_pnl=-0.0325
stress vol_spike_corr1: book_pnl=-0.0800

=== drawdown control (lagged) ===
uncontrolled maxDD=-0.750 controlled maxDD=-0.200 mean_exposure=0.040 days_flat=0

=== concentration & leverage limits ===
book0: max_w=0.292 gross=1.000 (limits w<=0.3 gross<=1.5)
book1: max_w=0.294 gross=1.000 (limits w<=0.3 gross<=1.5)
